  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM &#x2013; Multi Country Humanitarian Assistance &#x2013; CAP 2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For over 900,000 Rohingya in Bangladesh, 2022 will mark the fifth year since their mass displacement from Myanmar, preceded by decades of influxes spurred by systemic discrimination and targeted violence. Early leadership exercised by the Government of Bangladesh (GoB), with the support of the international community, worked to mitigate and manage the ensuing humanitarian crisis in the southern district of Cox&#x2019;s Bazar. Despite resilience and resolve shown by the refugee community, there will be no viable solution to the crisis until a safe and voluntary return to Rakhine State is guaranteed. While the GoB and the international community have maintained the provision of immediate lifesaving assistance, the Rohingya continue to face dangers posed by disasters related to natural hazards, disease outbreak, and a deteriorating protection environment. With this project, IOM continues its comprehensive humanitarian support for lifesaving assistance based on feedback from communities on what they need by providing comprehensive support to the vulnerable refugee and host community in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar through Site Management Engineering Project (SMEP), Protection, Site Management and Site Development (SMSD), health, and Needs and Population Monitoring (NMP).</narrative>
  </description>
